resyncType.description:
This field is for the "Line Quality Diagnostic" test only. It is mandatory for that test.
  - "No Resync" - the test will run without resynchronisation;
  - "Normal" - the test will run with resynchronisation in Normal Initialisation mode, collecting the HLOG and QLN;
  - "Robust" - the test will run with resynchronisation in Robust Initialisation mode, collecting the HLOG and QLN and provide a longer initialisation time with less strict parameters;

parameters.description:
(Conditional) Existing Service ID for Service Transfer. Either the entire AVC # (e.g. AVC000000000000) or the last 5 digits only (e.g 00000). `serviceRef` is accepted too.

Mandatory for, and only relevant to, Service Transfer orders.

Requires `customer_authority_date` to be supplied as well; a `service_ref` without one is rejected with a 400.

If specified, the response indicates the matching resource via `serviceIDMatch` on the copper line resources (FTTB / FTTN / FTTC) or on the NTD's `uniPortD` ports (FTTP / HFC / Fixed Wireless). Exactly one carries `true` when the AVC validates.

Any issues with validating the Service ID match are indicated via the `siteRestrictionError` object on the `siteRestriction`. These issues include:

 - RJ002003 - The provided AVC does not exist: {AVC}
 - RJ002004 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected: {AVC}
 - RJ002005 - The provided AVC exists at a different location: {AVC}
 - RJ002006 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected at a different location: {AVC}

post.description:
>**Required Scope(s):** voice:create

Puts one of your active numbers on the plan. From then on it can send and
receive faxes, and it has no separate monthly number charge.

Refused with `422` when:
  - the number is already on a fax plan (move it instead);
  - the plan is a Fax Bundle that already has its one number;
  - the plan is for an end user and the number is not on that end user's
    services;
  - the plan is closed.

delete.description:
>**Required Scope(s):** voice:update

Stop the link working at once. A used link cannot be cancelled (`409`);
cancelling one already cancelled answers `200` with it.

>**Required Scope(s):** data:update

Stop the link working at once. A used link cannot be cancelled (`409`);
cancelling one already cancelled answers `200` with it.

NbnSiteRestrictionError.description:
nbn's refusal of a qualification item, as nbn sends it. On a Service Transfer check, the reason the `serviceRef` did not validate:

 - RJ002003 - The provided AVC does not exist: {AVC}
 - RJ002004 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected: {AVC}
 - RJ002005 - The provided AVC exists at a different location: {AVC}
 - RJ002006 - The provided AVC has recently been disconnected at a different location: {AVC}
